---
import ServicePage from '@/layouts/ServicePage.astro';
import { site } from '@/data/site';
const description =
  'Terms for using our free calculators: results are estimates for planning, not professional advice; permitted use and embedding; limits of liability.';
---

<ServicePage title="Terms of use" {description} path="/terms/" h1="Terms of use" updated={new Date('2026-09-30')}>
  <p>By using {site.name} you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the site.</p>

  <h2>Results are estimates</h2>
  <p>Our calculators are tested carefully, but they rely on the inputs you enter and on assumptions that are shown on each page. Results are provided for planning and educational purposes. Confirm material quantities with your supplier, pay and tax figures with your employer or a tax professional, and health figures with a qualified clinician. We are not responsible for decisions made based on a result.</p>

  <h2>No professional advice</h2>
  <p>Nothing on this site is financial, legal, tax, medical or engineering advice. Pages on those topics are reviewed by professionals to be accurate in general, not to address your specific situation.</p>

  <h2>Permitted use</h2>
  <p>You may use the calculators for personal and commercial purposes and link to any page. You may not copy the site's text or code to another website, scrape the site at scale, or remove attribution from embedded widgets where we provide them.</p>

  <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
  <p>We may change, suspend or remove any calculator at any time. We try to keep the site available but do not guarantee uninterrupted access.</p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>To the fullest extent permitted by law, {site.name} and its contributors are not liable for any indirect, incidental or consequential damages, or for any loss arising from your use of the site or reliance on any result. Our total liability for any claim is limited to $100.</p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the United States and the state in which the site operator is established, without regard to conflict-of-law rules.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about these terms: <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
</ServicePage>
